.TH GLOBVER 1 "2026-07-30" "Selever" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
globver \- expose Selever-managed executables in the user's bin directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B globver use node
.I version
.br
.B globver use npm
.I package[@version]
.RI [ \-\-node= version ]
.br
.B globver use go
.I version
.br
.B globver use gopkg
.I package[@version]
.RI [ \-\-go= version ]
.br
.B globver use dotnet
.I package[@version]
.br
.B globver remove node
.br
.B globver remove npm
.I package
.br
.B globver remove go
.br
.B globver remove gopkg
.I package
.br
.B globver remove dotnet
.I package
.br
.B globver list
.br
.B globver install
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B globver
installs selections through Selever and creates launchers in
.IR $HOME/.local/bin .
Each launcher uses an executable's native name, adds the directories required
by its recorded selection to
.BR PATH ,
and runs the installed executable.
.PP
The configuration records exact selectors by executable name.
Launchers contain resolved absolute paths and do not read the configuration
when they run.
.B globver
marks its launchers and refuses to overwrite a file without that marker.
.SH USE COMMANDS
.B globver use
resolves the requested selection, installs it, records every executable it
owns, and writes the launchers.
It prints the exact recorded selection and the executable names to standard
error.
.TP
.BI "use node " version
Expose every executable in a Node.js release.
.I version
may be exact,
.BR latest ,
a one-, two-, or three-part numeric prefix, or an LTS codename.
Exact versions are used without metadata resolution.
.TP
.BI "use npm " package[@version] " [\-\-node=" version ]
Expose every executable owned by an npm package.
The package version may be a numeric prefix or dist-tag and defaults to
.BR latest .
The Node.js version may use the same queries as
.BR "globver use node" .
.TP
.BI "use go " version
Expose every executable in an exact Go release.
The version must not have a leading
.BR go .
.TP
.BI "use gopkg " package[@version] " [\-\-go=" version ]
Expose every executable produced by a Go package.
The package version may be any Go module version query and defaults to
.BR latest .
The Go version must be exact.
.TP
.BI "use dotnet " package[@version]
Expose every command provided by a dotnet tool package.
The version may be
.B latest
or a one-, two-, or three-part stable prefix and defaults to
.BR latest .
The package is installed, or updated when necessary, by
.BR "dotnet tool"
as a global tool.
.SH PARENT TOOLCHAINS
npm selections record an exact Node.js version, and Go package selections
record an exact Go version.
.PP
When
.B \-\-node
or
.B \-\-go
is omitted and standard input and output are terminals,
.B globver
opens a searchable list of completed local installations.
When the streams are not terminals, it uses the recorded global
.B node
or
.B go
selection.
The command fails if no suitable local or recorded selection is available.
.SH REMOVE COMMANDS
.B globver remove
deletes every managed launcher owned by the named selection and removes its
configuration entries.
The argument identifies a selector, not an executable name.
.TP
.B remove node
Remove the recorded Node.js selection.
.TP
.BI "remove npm " package
Remove the recorded npm package selection.
.TP
.B remove go
Remove the recorded Go selection.
.TP
.BI "remove gopkg " package
Remove the recorded Go package selection.
.TP
.BI "remove dotnet " package
Remove the recorded dotnet tool selection and uninstall the global dotnet tool.
The package name is matched without regard to case.
.PP
Installed Selever data is retained when a Node.js, npm, Go, or Go package
selection is removed.
.SH OTHER COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Write a table of exact recorded selections and their executable names to
standard output.
Executables that share a selection are grouped on one row.
.TP
.B install
Install every recorded selection and recreate its managed launchers.
This command is suitable for restoring the configured commands on another
machine after copying
.IR global.json .
It refuses to replace unmanaged files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration is a JSON object whose keys are executable names and whose
values are exact selector argument arrays.
For example:
.PP
.EX
{
  "tsc": ["npm", "typescript@5.8.2", "--node", "22.14.0"],
  "tsserver": ["npm", "typescript@5.8.2", "--node", "22.14.0"]
}
.EE
.PP
Configuration changes and launcher changes are serialized with an exclusive
lock.
The configuration file is replaced atomically.
.SH OUTPUT
.B globver use
writes the resolved selection and sorted executable names to standard error:
.PP
.EX
selection: npm typescript@5.8.2 --node 22.14.0
executables: tsc, tsserver
.EE
.PP
.B globver list
writes a table to standard output:
.PP
.EX
SELECTION                                      EXECUTABLES
npm pnpm@9.15.9 --node 22.23.1                pnpm, pnpx
npm typescript@5.8.2 --node 22.14.0           tsc, tsserver
.EE
.PP
Installation progress and diagnostics are written to standard error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Locates
.IR .local/bin
and the default configuration, data, and cache directories.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the configuration directory base.
The default is
.IR $HOME/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Overrides the Selever data directory base.
The default is
.IR $HOME/.local/share .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Overrides the Selever cache directory base.
The default is
.IR $HOME/.cache .
.TP
.B DOTNET_CLI_HOME
Changes the home directory used by dotnet, including the location of its global
tool executables.
.TP
.B GOPROXY
Controls Go module lookup for Go package selection and installation.
.TP
.B HTTP_PROXY, HTTPS_PROXY, NO_PROXY
Control proxies for version metadata and download requests.
.TP
.B PATH
Used to locate
.B go
during Go package resolution and
.B dotnet
for dotnet tool operations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:\-$HOME/.config}/selever/global.json
Exact selections indexed by executable name.
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:\-$HOME/.config}/selever/global.json.lock
Configuration lock file.
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/bin
Managed executable launchers.
.TP
.I ${XDG_DATA_HOME:\-$HOME/.local/share}/selever
Selever-managed toolchain and package installations.
.TP
.I ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:\-$HOME/.cache}/selever
Downloaded metadata, archives, and package-manager caches.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B globver
exits with status 0 when the requested configuration and launchers are in
place, a selection is removed, or the list is written.
Canceling an interactive parent-toolchain selector also exits with status 0.
Other errors produce a non-zero status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Select the newest stable Node.js 22 release:
.PP
.EX
globver use node 22
.EE
.PP
Expose TypeScript using an explicit Node.js release:
.PP
.EX
globver use npm typescript@latest --node 22.14.0
.EE
.PP
Use the recorded global Go release to build and expose gopls in a
non-interactive invocation:
.PP
.EX
globver use gopkg golang.org/x/tools/gopls@latest
.EE
.PP
Remove every launcher owned by the TypeScript selection:
.PP
.EX
globver remove npm typescript
.EE
.SH NOTES
Node.js and Go archives are checksum-verified.
npm retains its native integrity and lifecycle behavior.
Dotnet packages are managed in the dotnet global tool store; Globver manages
launchers for their commands.
.PP
Supported platforms are macOS and glibc Linux on amd64 and arm64.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR selever (1),
.BR fetchver (1),
.BR dotnet-tool (1)
